Schematic diagram:
	Line-Sensors:
		For detecting the line field borders we use phototransistors which are detecting reflected light from the filed. If out robot moves over white border line we detect voltage change in our sensors.  


	Use of multiplexors:
		Since arduino mega has limited amount of analog inputs. We decided to use multiplexors for LINE and IR sensors.

	Camera:
		We use pixy cam V2 which is connected to arduino via ISCP pins.




The biggest problem we had was with ball detection. In the first desgns we didin`t have any reference materials on how to detect balls location reliably. We were trying many different solutions and one thing that helped us was that we switched out TSOP sensors from 40kHz dection freqeuncy to 38kHz. This was counter intuitive for us becouse the ball emits IR pusles at 40kHz. The reason this helped us was that the TSOP sensors were sensing light reflections from all the different surfaces and we couldn`t procces the ball angle. Since then we spoke with differnt teams and one of them helped us with their solution to add low pass filter to the output so that small errors could be eliminated.



With our new PCB designs we decited to switch from Teensy 4.1 to Arduino Mega. We reasoned this downgrade in processing power by reliability a simplicity of our communication mainly with  motor drivers. Since Teensy 4 microcontrollers run on 3,3V and our motor drivers use 5V logic we had to use logic voltage converters which didnt work as expected. Working with arduino Mega is much simpler and reliable.



